WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.742
you seen a man with red hair?"

2
00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:16.642
said Dr.

3
00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:19.044
Dolittle. "What's his ship called?"

4
00:00:19.644 --> 00:00:20.465
asked a dolphin.

5
00:00:20.865 --> 00:00:22.486
"The Saucy Sally.

6
00:00:22.626 --> 00:00:23.867
Please find him."

7
00:00:26.209 --> 00:00:28.570
Dr. Dolittle waited for the dolphins.

8
00:00:29.271 --> 00:00:32.076
"We found the boat," one dolphin said.

9
00:00:32.096 --> 00:00:35.277
"But there was no one inside," said the other.

10
00:00:35.297 --> 00:00:39.878
"And we didn't find any body in the water," said the first one.

11
00:00:39.898 --> 00:00:43.239
"He is not in the ocean," the second one said.

12
00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.961
Dr. Dolittle told the boy what the dolphins said.

13
00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:50.261
"My uncle is alive!"

14
00:00:51.161 --> 00:00:52.662
The boy clapped his hands.

15
00:00:53.642 --> 00:00:55.423
All the animals were happy too.

16
00:00:55.903 --> 00:00:57.583
They danced and sang together.

17
00:01:03.684 --> 00:01:05.806
After eating a big meal, Dr.

18
00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:10.450
Dolittle said: "Now we must continue to search for your uncle."

19
00:01:11.231 --> 00:01:15.094
"Dr. Dolittle, ask the eagles," Dab-Dab whispered.

20
00:01:15.695 --> 00:01:17.997
"Eagles can see better than any other creature."

21
00:01:19.518 --> 00:01:22.461
Dr. Dolittle called and spoke with two eagles.

22
00:01:23.081 --> 00:01:24.663
Eagles don't like to talk much.

23
00:01:25.223 --> 00:01:27.285
But they agreed to help the good doctor.

24
00:01:27.305 --> 00:01:30.368
"We'll be back," one said in a deep voice.

25
00:01:34.276 --> 00:01:36.718
That evening, the eagles returned to the ship.

26
00:01:36.738 --> 00:01:38.640
"We searched everywhere.

27
00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:42.263
But this man is nowhere to be seen," said one eagle.

28
00:01:42.903 --> 00:01:44.604
The other one didn't say a word.

29
00:01:44.624 --> 00:01:48.127
"He is not on land," continued the eagle.

30
00:01:48.788 --> 00:01:50.749
They bowed their heads and flew off.

31
00:01:52.991 --> 00:01:55.293
Dr. Dolittle did not know what to do.

32
00:01:55.313 --> 00:01:57.995
"But he must be alive!"

33
00:01:58.515 --> 00:01:59.036
he said.

34
00:01:59.056 --> 00:02:02.999
"Let me try to find him, Doctor," Jip offered.

35
00:02:03.019 --> 00:02:05.942
"You? How can YOU find him?"

36
00:02:07.323 --> 00:02:08.244
laughed Gub-Gub.

37
00:02:08.264 --> 00:02:14.069
"Dogs have a great sense of smell," Jip growled.

38
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.772
The other animals laughed at Jip.

39
00:02:17.792 --> 00:02:22.836
"Dolphins and eagles are the smartest creatures," Dab-Dab pointed out.

40
00:02:23.557 --> 00:02:24.638
"They couldn't find him.

41
00:02:24.918 --> 00:02:25.919
So how can you?"

42
00:02:25.939 --> 00:02:27.961
"I'll find the uncle!"

43
00:02:28.461 --> 00:02:29.102
Jip barked.

44
00:02:29.122 --> 00:02:31.284
"Just you wait and see!"

45
00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.601
Jip spoke quietly to the doctor.

46
00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:38.362
"Do you have something of your uncle's?"

47
00:02:38.882 --> 00:02:40.463
Dr. Dolittle asked the boy.

48
00:02:40.483 --> 00:02:44.985
"Only this," the boy took out a red handkerchief.

49
00:02:45.805 --> 00:02:48.026
Jip sniffed and smelled the handkerchief.

50
00:02:48.046 --> 00:02:52.368
"I smell pickles and lemons," Jip said.

51
00:02:53.709 --> 00:02:58.611
Dr. Dolittle asked the boy: "Does your uncle like pickles and lemons?"

52
00:02:59.351 --> 00:03:01.232
"Yes! How did you know?"

53
00:03:02.088 --> 00:03:03.469
The boy was surprised.

54
00:03:03.489 --> 00:03:07.272
"He carries them in a jar and eats them all the time."

55
00:03:09.774 --> 00:03:13.016
Everyone watched as Jip smelled and smelled the air.

56
00:03:13.036 --> 00:03:18.940
"Onions, wet raincoats, burning leaves," Jip mumbled.

57
00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.483
"Can you really smell all those things?"

58
00:03:22.983 --> 00:03:24.224
Dr. Dolittle asked.

59
00:03:24.244 --> 00:03:25.785
"Of course!

60
00:03:26.446 --> 00:03:29.288
The wind carries the smell," Jip replied.

61
00:03:31.108 --> 00:03:32.449
Many hours went by.

62
00:03:32.469 --> 00:03:36.713
"He's not going to find the uncle," Gub-Gub sighed.

63
00:03:36.733 --> 00:03:38.354
"Let's go and eat."

64
00:03:39.155 --> 00:03:41.717
Suddenly, Jip let out a sharp cry.

65
00:03:41.737 --> 00:03:43.438
"Pickles and lemons!

66
00:03:43.878 --> 00:03:44.399
Over there!"
